# Finevines Go build (cmd/finevines)
.env
dist/
finevines.exe
*.exe

# .bunny-manifest.json is deliberately TRACKED, not ignored. It is the hash of
# every file currently on Bunny.net, and it is what makes `deploy` upload only
# what changed. CI checks out fresh every run, so an untracked manifest would
# make every nightly run re-upload the whole site and purge the CDN. The
# pipeline commits it back after each deploy.

# Per-run scratch state for the CI pipeline (before-snapshot for the digest,
# the applied-action log). Written by one run, read by `notify` later in the
# SAME run, never committed.
.run/

# Editor workspace file (personal, not shared)
*.code-workspace

# Salesforce Enterprise WSDL (exposes full custom schema — keep out of history)
docs/salesforce/*.wsdl

# Enrichment coverage report (generated, internal — never published to the CDN)
# (reports/* rather than reports/ — git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# DIRECTORY is excluded, so the negation below would be dead.)
reports/*
# image-coverage.md is the one exception: generated, but COMMITTED, because it
# is the figure the cutover checklist and the supplier ask are quoted from, and
# a number nobody can diff is a number nobody trusts. Without this, `git add
# reports/image-coverage.md` exits 1 even though the file is already tracked.
!reports/image-coverage.md

# Generated ChatGPT enrichment prompt batches (regenerable from the roster)
data/enrichment-prompts/
data/enrichment-prompts.md

# Raw ChatGPT enrichment pastes (transient; ingested into data/enrichment/)
out-*.json

# Generated wine label SVGs (~2,200). `finevines build` regenerates any that are
# missing (internal/build.ensureLabels), so these are a build artifact, not
# source. The matched bottle PHOTOGRAPHS (.jpg, ~478) are NOT reproducible —
# they came from the old site and external URLs — and stay tracked.
# (The 33 demo-seed-era .svg files once tracked here, plus ~1,836 more sitting
# untracked in the working tree, were the retired invented-label artwork;
# both groups were deleted 2026-08-09 — none was referenced by a current wine.)
assets/img/wines/*.svg

# bottlecomp scratch output (tools/bottlecomp -outdir)
out-bottle/

# gpt-image-1 dry-run output (tools/imagedryrun -out)
out-imagedryrun/

# Staged bottle photographs from tools/labelfetch (review before importing)
data/fetched-images/

# Verifier/normaliser binaries (built from tools/)
imgcheck.exe
imgnorm.exe

# Scratch from the pre-cutover audit: raw HTML pulled off the old site while
# capturing its privacy/legal copy (the text that mattered is committed under
# data/legal/), and an old gpt-image-1 dry-run output directory. Neither is
# load-bearing; both otherwise show up as hundreds of untracked files.
data/oldsite-fetched/
out-imagedryrun-high/
